Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/packet-net/axcall
Description: SOCKS5 proxy onto an AX.25 port
 Puts a SOCKS5 proxy in front of one AX.25 port. Every connection it accepts
 becomes a connected-mode AX.25 session to a callsign, and the bytes pass
 through untouched, so curl, ssh, browsers and any HTTP library reach a packet
 station over an ordinary socket without knowing what AX.25 is.
 .
 The mapping is exact rather than approximate: a connected-mode AX.25 session
 is reliable, ordered and flow-controlled, and so is a TCP connection, so the
 proxy opens a link, copies bytes, and closes the link when they run out.
 Streams only; there is no UDP and no ping.
 .
 Carries its own AX.25 v2.2 data link and speaks KISS to a TNC over a serial
 port or over TCP, so it needs no kernel support, no kissattach and no
 privilege. Reads the same /etc/axcall/ports as axcall, plus an
 /etc/axcall/hosts giving names to stations.
 .
 Self-contained: bundles its own .NET runtime, so no system runtime is
 required.

