SHA1: b67edaaaffda12a035a6f3e87c5b8147e408c705
SHA256: d875fc1cfcc3054210910f8b5721709b5624f075fc35797fbece030d196bc5c3
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/packet-net/axcall
Description: IP over AX.25 on a TUN device
 Carries IP over an AX.25 radio channel on a TUN device, so software that
 already exists works over radio: ping, ssh, UDP, and a route to a remote
 site's whole LAN. None of that is reachable through a stream proxy, which is
 what axsocks and axinetd are.
 .
 Transmits IP in UI frames with PID 0xCC, because running IP inside a reliable
 ARQ link sets two retransmission timers against the same loss and wrecks TCP's
 round trip estimate. Accepts IP either way on receive, since both are
 configured in the field. Answers AX.25 ARP, so a station that has not been
 told about this one can still find it. Everything goes direct: layer 2
 digipeating is not done here, so stations behind a repeater are not reachable.
 .
 Filters what goes out, and starts closed. An unfiltered IP interface on a
 shared channel transmits mDNS, SSDP, NetBIOS and DHCP renewals unasked, under
 the operator's personal licence; nothing is transmitted here that no rule
 allows.
 .
 Carries its own AX.25 layer and speaks KISS to a TNC over a serial port or
 over TCP, so it needs no kernel AX.25 stack and no kissattach. Creating the
 interface needs CAP_NET_ADMIN; given a persistent device created in advance it
 runs unprivileged.
 .
 Self-contained: bundles its own .NET runtime, so no system runtime is
 required.

